; Coordinated attack with two generals ga and gb. Random first decides whether ga plans to attack.
; Only ga learns the plan. Then four messages alternate ga to gb, gb to ga, ga to gb, gb to ga.
; A general only sends message k after receiving message k minus 1, and random delivers or drops every message.
; k1 to k4 are the nested knowledge levels: k1 is gb knows attack, k2 is ga knows k1, and so on.
; ck is common knowledge of the plan and is never reached over the unreliable channel.
;@instructions THE TWO GENERALS
;@instructions A random setup chooses attack or hold. Only general ga learns the plan.
;@instructions The generals send four acknowledgements in turn. Each message may be delivered or dropped; a general can send only after receiving the previous message.
;@instructions Follow the nested knowledge predicates k1 through k4 with queries such as :q gb k1. Even four acknowledgements do not make the plan common knowledge (ck).

(role ga)
(role gb)
(role random)

(sender 1 ga) (sender 2 gb) (sender 3 ga) (sender 4 gb)
(receiver 1 gb) (receiver 2 ga) (receiver 3 gb) (receiver 4 ga)
(pred 1 0) (pred 2 1) (pred 3 2) (pred 4 3)
(succ 0 1) (succ 1 2) (succ 2 3) (succ 3 4) (succ 4 5)

(init (round 0))
(init (recv 0))

(<= (legal random (decide ?p)) (true (round 0)) (planOption ?p))
(planOption attack) (planOption hold)
(<= (legal random deliver) (not (true (round 0))))
(<= (legal random drop) (not (true (round 0))))
(<= (legal ?g noop) (role ?g) (distinct ?g random) (true (round 0)))

(<= (canSend ?s) (true (round ?k)) (sender ?k ?s) (pred ?k ?j) (true (recv ?j)))
(<= (legal ?s send) (canSend ?s))
(<= (legal ?g noop) (role ?g) (distinct ?g random) (not (true (round 0))) (not (canSend ?g)))

(<= (next (plan ?p)) (does random (decide ?p)))
(<= (next (plan ?p)) (true (plan ?p)))
(<= (next (round ?n)) (true (round ?m)) (succ ?m ?n))
(<= (next (recv ?k)) (true (round ?k)) (sender ?k ?s) (does ?s send) (does random deliver))
(<= (next (recv ?k)) (true (recv ?k)))

(<= (sees ga (plan ?p)) (does random (decide ?p)))
(<= (sees ?r (msg ?k ?p)) (true (round ?k)) (sender ?k ?s) (receiver ?k ?r) (does ?s send) (does random deliver) (true (plan ?p)))

(<= attack (true (plan attack)))
(<= (k1) (knows gb attack))
(<= (k2) (knows ga k1))
(<= (k3) (knows gb k2))
(<= (k4) (knows ga k3))
(<= (ck) (knows attack))

(<= (terminal) (true (round 5)))
(goal ga 100) (goal gb 100) (goal random 0)
